    "lineage agent notes: The ROW_NUMBER at lines 76-77 groups by (period, claim_id) only, not by reserve_type. So each claim keeps just its single latest reserve row, whatever its type. The header says expense reserves count towards incurred (CR-0577), but they are only included when the expense reserve happens to be the latest row. The SUM at lines 85-86 then always adds up exactly one row per period. The PySpark version must copy this exactly, not fix it. Ties on reserve_date are broken by reserve_id DESC.\n\nWhen computing last_payment_date, payments with a NULL amount are skipped (line 67), but they still count as nil in the sums.\n\ndays_since_last_activity is NULL when the claim has no payments and no reserves. The 1900-01-01 sentinel only affects the comparison and never reaches the output.\n\nThe filter edges on payment_date, reserve_date and the claim_id joins in the payment and reserve steps decide which payment and reserve rows feed the sums. They change which rows appear only indirectly, through the incurred_amount >= 25000 threshold at line 134."
